## Setup

```bash
python3 -m venv .venv && .venv/bin/pip install "google-adk[eval]>=2.12,<3" pytest pytest-asyncio python-dotenv
cp .env.example .env    # then fill in the project and location
gcloud auth application-default login
```

## Run

```bash
adk run {{APP_NAME}} --jsonl "a request to try"
adk web .                       # dev UI, with the trace and eval tabs
```

## Evaluate

```bash
# deterministic, gates every change
adk eval {{APP_NAME}} tests/eval/evalsets/happy.evalset.json \
    --config_file_path tests/eval/eval_config.json

# the honest gate: AgentEvaluator raises, so the exit code means something
pytest tests/eval -v
```

`adk eval` always exits 0, even when cases fail. Use pytest, or
`/adk:eval-run`, anywhere the result has to gate something.

## Layout

```
{{APP_NAME}}/          the agent package: agent.py, tools.py, schemas.py
tests/eval/            eval_config.json, evalsets/, test_eval.py
.env.example           backend and MODEL_NAME
```
